  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Lakshey Garg vs State Of Punjab on 7 March, 2019 Author: Rajbir Sehrawat Bench: Rajbir Sehrawat 211 In The High Court Of Punjab And Haryana At Chandigarh Crm-M-5128-2019 (O&M) Date of decision:07.03.2019 Lakshey Garg ...Petitioner Versus State of Punjab ...Respondent Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Rajbir Sehrawat Present: Mr. Atul Goyal, Advocate for the petitioner. Mr. K.S.Aulakh, Dag, Punjab. ** * * * Rajbir Sehrawat, J. (Oral) Prayer in this petition filed under Section 439 of Cr.P.C. is for grant of bail pending trial in case Fir No.141 dated 10.12.2018 under Sections 272, 273, 420, 465, 467, 472, 473 of Ipc and Sections 59/63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, registered at Police Station Cantt. Bathinda, District Bathinda.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner contends that the petitioner has been wrongly involved in this case. The petitioner is not involved in any business activity of any kind whatsoever. Rather, the petitioner is a student of 12th Class. The petitioner has been involved in this case only because of the reason that he was driving a car in which his father was travelling. The allegation is that from the said car, spurious ghee was recovered. But, it is only father of the petitioner, who would know about the business aspect of any article lying in the car. The petitioner is in custody since 10.12.2018. The investigation of the case qua the petitioner is already complete and he is not required for any investigation purposes. 1 On the other hand, learned State counsel, being instructed by ASI Rajinderpal Singh, submits that the petitioner was found driving the car in which spurious ghee was transported. It is further submitted that from the factory owned by the father of the petitioner, chemicals and stickers meant for preparing and selling the spurious ghee were recovered.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner contends that the petitioner has been wrongly involved in this case. The petitioner is not involved in any business activity of any kind whatsoever. Rather, the petitioner is a student of 12th Class. The petitioner has been involved in this case only because of the reason that he was driving a car in which his father was travelling. The allegation is that from the said car, spurious ghee was recovered. But, it is only father of the petitioner, who would know about the business aspect of any article lying in the car. The petitioner is in custody since 10.12.2018. The investigation of the case qua the petitioner is already complete and he is not required for any investigation purposes. 1 On the other hand, learned State counsel, being instructed by ASI Rajinderpal Singh, submits that the petitioner was found driving the car in which spurious ghee was transported. It is further submitted that from the factory owned by the father of the petitioner, chemicals and stickers meant for preparing and selling the spurious ghee were recovered.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
